<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:46:25 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo Ebola outbreak 'growing exponentially' with more than 2,500 dead</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-dr-congo-ebola-outbreak-growing-exponentially-with-more-than-2-500-dead</link><description>
The Ebola outbreak raging in the Democratic Republic of Congo is growing "exponentially", with more than 2,500 deaths recorded and half of those in the last 20 days, the senior UN coordinator on the disease said Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">837f67ba-9d54-11f1-9288-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30aa3c84-927a-11f1-8c5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4c0d8f36aaec52efd39cb5a048c64eb1b85d0d42.jpg">© Jospin Mwisha / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France backs down on plan to make patients pay more for healthcare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-france-backs-down-on-plan-to-make-patients-pay-more-for-healthcare-medicine</link><description>
The French government has scrapped plans to double the annual ceiling on out-of-pocket charges for medicines, medical appointments and other healthcare, after criticism from patient groups and health professionals. The cap was due to rise from €100 to €200, but the government will instead pursue a smaller increase linked to inflation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">264a2d16-9d52-11f1-8885-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:45:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg">AP - Daniel Cole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and European allies press Israel to abandon West Bank settlement plan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-france-and-european-allies-press-israel-to-abandon-west-bank-settlement-plan</link><description>
France has joined Germany, Italy and the United Kingdom in calling on Israel to halt the expansion of settlements illegal under international law in the occupied West Bank, and immediately withdraw tenders issued this week for more than 1,200 new homes under the controversial E1 project.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8e5c86c-9d29-11f1-b0f3-e1f7ae7eac67</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:01:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg">©  OHAD ZWIGENBERG / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Cameroon’s President Biya home after 73-day absence, amid health speculation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260821-cameroon-president-biya-home-after-73-day-absence-amid-health-speculation</link><description>
Cameroon’s President Paul Biya has returned to the country after spending 73 days abroad, ending an unusually long absence that has intensified speculation around the 93-year-old’s health and raised questions over Cameroon's political future.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff0dfbf0-9d34-11f1-a29e-831a4ab27004</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:11:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/30b5a8f0-8b43-11f1-b9d1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP-Sunday-Alamba-1.jpg">AP - Sunday Alamba</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Millions in France report eco-anxiety after summer of heatwaves and wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-millions-in-france-report-eco-anxiety-after-summer-of-heat-and-wildfires</link><description>
Record-breaking heatwaves, drought and wildfires are driving a surge in eco-anxiety across France, with some sufferers "paralysed" by panic attacks, unable to work and, in the most severe cases, experiencing suicidal thoughts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cfa3812-9c8e-11f1-9c7e-2f8d63b40800</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 05:59:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg">AP - Claude Paris</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UN holds second informal straw poll for next leader</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-un-holds-second-informal-poll-for-next-leader</link><description>
The UN's most powerful body, the Security Council, meets Friday to hold another straw poll to gauge the popularity of a growing field of contenders to lead the embattled organisation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5382de70-9cff-11f1-bbac-cbbe5bb185af</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 01:26:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg">© Leonardo MUNOZ / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Deadly border mine collapse exposes risks behind Central Africa's gold rush</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-deadly-border-mine-collapse-exposes-risks-behind-central-africa-s-gold-rush-zamboye</link><description>
A deadly landslide at a gold mine on the Cameroon-Central African Republic border has triggered calls for greater oversight of mining operations, after dozens of people were killed and many more were reported missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49f67a2a-9c90-11f1-ab31-a5221940408f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:47:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/aa4723ae-7a99-11ef-9f4c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Gaga-mines-or.jpg">© RFI/Rolf Steve Domia-Leu</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>West Bank village siege fuels concern over growing settler violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-west-bank-village-siege-fuels-concern-over-growing-settler-violence-qusra</link><description>
Palestinian families remained trapped in their homes in the occupied West Bank village of Qusra for an 11th day on Thursday, in a case that has drawn condemnation from US Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee and become a symbol of growing settler violence in the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f68c4d44-9ca1-11f1-918c-f35507a1bea8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg">AFP - ZAIN JAAFAR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Spain to open shelters in Ceuta for migrants and transfer 500 girls to mainland</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-spain-to-open-shelters-in-ceuta-for-migrants-and-transfer-500-girls-to-mainland</link><description>
Spain will open temporary shelters for up to 1,800 migrants in Ceuta, its enclave in Morocco, as authorities tackle the humanitarian crisis resulting from tens of thousands of people attempting to enter the territory last month. The government is also preparing to transfer 500 unaccompanied migrant girls to mainland Spain, despite opposition from Ceuta authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b17bfa10-9c83-11f1-8237-a5c3347b2fe8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:45:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French hospital helicopter landings disrupted by illegal prison delivery drones</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-french-hospital-helicopter-landings-disrupted-by-illegal-prison-delivery-drones</link><description>
Emergency helicopter landings at Strasbourg University Hospitals have been suspended over the risk of collision with drones used to illegally deliver items to inmates in a nearby prison. The hospital says the resulting detour could be "life-threatening" for patients.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cbfa0aba-9c99-11f1-89cd-cf462987716b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:09:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg">© Gabriel BOUYS / AFP/Archives</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Five years on from first vaccine, fight against malaria sees progress in Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-five-years-on-from-first-vaccine-fight-against-malaria-sees-progress-in-africa</link><description>
On World Mosquito Day, attention remains focused on the devastating impact of the disease in Africa. The continent accounts for 95 per cent of malaria-related deaths worldwide. Five years after the roll-out of the first malaria vaccine, it is beginning to deliver measurable results – although significant challenges remain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e5f87ce-9c92-11f1-bc8c-81338d49049e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:23:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b09af880-9c6f-11f1-a353-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25230427734255.jpg">© AP - Patrick Onen</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rights group calls for release of two French journalists held in Togo</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260820-rights-group-calls-for-release-of-two-french-journalists-held-in-togo-ga%C3%ABl-moca%C3%ABr-sebastian-perez-pezzani</link><description>
Two French journalists detained in Togo since late July have been placed in pre-trial detention and charged with "false statements", Reporters Without Borders (RSF) has said, calling for their immediate release. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e36a440-9c75-11f1-a3a4-815bbe2c6f6d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:19:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/256d789e-68cb-11ee-ba4d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Chu_%281%29.jpg">© Theolebaron/WikiCommons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French winegrowers begin record early harvest as heat and drought bite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-record-early-grape-harvest-in-france-highlights-growing-impact-of-climate-change</link><description>
Drought and heatwaves have pushed French winegrowers to start picking grapes weeks ahead of schedule, with this year seeing some of the earliest harvests on record – a sign of how climate change is reshaping the wine calendar across the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31807718-9a4f-11f1-af8a-39f218d346d1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 04:41:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg">© Sarah Meyssonnier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>July heatwave sees 1,243 deaths in France, bringing summer toll to 7,300</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-july-heatwave-caused-over-1-200-deaths-in-france-bringing-summer-toll-to-7-300</link><description>
More than 1,200 excess deaths were recorded in France during the country's July heatwave, bringing the provisional death toll from extreme temperatures this year to 7,300.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369b69e8-9c5b-11f1-9fd0-11ad03b15a71</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 05:51:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg">© Tom Nicholson/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Twenty years after Probo Koala, Africa still grapples with ‘waste colonialism’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-twenty-years-after-probo-koala-africa-still-grapples-with-waste-colonialism-abidjan</link><description>
Twenty years after toxic waste from the cargo ship Probo Koala was dumped across Abidjan in Côte d'Ivoire, the disaster remains an open wound for many victims and a symbol of wealthy countries sending unwanted waste to Africa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">078fe796-9ba2-11f1-acad-6748bf4168d5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:02:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7ab2f0c-9b81-11f1-aa59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par942011.jpg">AFP - RAIGO PAJULA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Liberia to take in up to 1,200 US deportees within a year</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-liberia-to-take-in-up-to-1-200-us-deportees-within-a-year</link><description>
Liberia has announced it will receive up to 1,200 foreign nationals deported from the United States – one of the largest known deals struck with African countries as part of President Donald Trump's unprecedented bid to drive out undocumented migrants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b27abf02-9bbe-11f1-995b-7bd032427e98</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:44:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4604c40-f77f-11f0-a0a9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-923W4W2.jpg">AFP - OCTAVIO JONES</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigeria election campaign begins as voters grapple with inflation crisis</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260819-nigeria-election-campaign-begins-as-voters-grapple-with-inflation-crisis</link><description>
Campaigning kicks off in Nigeria Wednesday, five months ahead of elections set to be dominated by crushing inflation and President Bola Tinubu's economic reforms.
